      "message": "With dexpreopt config changes it is also good to run a first boot time check to see if the dexpreopt artifacts are ok (if something goes off at build time, precompiled files may be rejected at boot time and presubmit won\u0027t show that).\n\nCan you run this boot time test:\n\nIn one terminal, build, flash and boot (I normally use launch_cvd on cuttlefish to avoid flashing, e.g. aosp_cf_x86_64_phone-userdebug target).\n\nIn another terminal, grep first boot logcat for messages:\n\n  $ adb wait-for-device \\\n    \u0026\u0026 adb -s $S root \\\n    \u0026\u0026 adb -s $S logcat \\\n    | grep -E \u0027ClassLoaderContext [a-z ]+ mismatch\u0027 -C 1\n\nThe output should not contain any error messages.\n\nSpoiler: I just tried that myself with your CLs and it works (no errors), but if you keep working on dexpreopt then this is the current way to see if it really works. On AOSP it should be clean, on internal master there are currently a few failures.",
